msgid "Logging configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Read about the use of logging API in {project-name}, configuring logging "
"output, and using logging adapters to unify the output from other logging "
"APIs."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This document is part of the xref:observability.adoc[Observability in "
"Quarkus reference guide] which features this and other observability related "
"components."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus uses the JBoss Log Manager logging backend for publishing "
"application and framework logs.\n"
"Quarkus supports the JBoss Logging API and multiple other logging APIs, "
"seamlessly integrated with JBoss Log Manager.\n"
"You can use any of the <<logging-apis,following APIs>>:"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:https://github.com/jboss-logging/jboss-logging[JBoss Logging]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/java.logging/java/"
"util/logging/package-summary.html[JDK `java.util.logging` (JUL)]"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:https://www.slf4j.org/[SLF4J]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-logging/[Apache Commons "
"Logging]"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/[Apache Log4j 2]"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:https://logging.apache.org/log4j/1.2/[Apache Log4j 1]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use JBoss Logging for application logging"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using the JBoss Logging API, your application requires no additional "
"dependencies, as {project-name} automatically provides it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Get an application logger"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To get an application logger in {project-name}, select one of the following "
"approaches."
msgstr ""

msgid "<<declaring-a-logger-field>>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<<simplified-logging>>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<<injection-of-a-configured-logger>>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Declaring a logger field"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With this classic approach, you use a specific API to obtain a logger "
"instance, store it in a static field of a class, and call logging operations "
"upon this instance."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same flow can be applied with any of the <<logging-apis,supported "
"logging APIs>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Define the logger field."
msgstr ""

msgid "Invoke the desired logging methods on the `log` object."
msgstr ""

msgid "Simplified logging"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus simplifies logging by automatically adding logger fields to classes "
"that use `io.quarkus.logging.Log`.\n"
"This eliminates the need for repetitive boilerplate code and enhances "
"logging setup convenience."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `io.quarkus.logging.Log` class contains the same methods as JBoss "
"Logging, except that they are `static`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that the class does not declare a logger field.\n"
"This is because during application build, a `private static final org.jboss."
"logging.Logger` field is created automatically in each class that uses the "
"`Log` API.\n"
"The fully qualified name of the class that calls the `Log` methods is used "
"as a logger name.\n"
"In this example, the logger name would be `com.example.MyService`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Finally, all calls to `Log` methods are rewritten to regular JBoss Logging "
"calls on the logger field during the application build."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the `Log` API only in application classes, not in external dependencies.\n"
"`Log` method calls not processed by Quarkus at build time will result in an "
"exception."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using <code>io.quarkus.logging.Log</code> in extensions:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While the `Log` API simplifies logging in application classes, it is not "
"recommended for use in extension modules or external dependencies."
msgstr ""

msgid "The following considerations apply:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`io.quarkus.logging.Log` depends on Quarkus bytecode transformations that "
"occur at build time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In extension modules, `Log` works only if the module includes a Jandex index."
"\n"
"However, this behavior is unsupported and can lead to unreliable logging."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For extension development, use `org.jboss.logging.Logger.getLogger(String)` "
"instead of `io.quarkus.logging.Log`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Injecting a configured logger"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The injection of a configured `org.jboss.logging.Logger` logger instance "
"with the `@Inject` annotation is another alternative to adding an "
"application logger, but is applicable only to CDI beans."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use `@Inject Logger log`, where the logger gets named after the "
"class you inject it to, or `@Inject @LoggerName(\"...\") Logger log`, where "
"the logger will receive the specified name.\n"
"Once injected, you can use the `log` object to invoke logging methods."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The fully qualified class name (FQCN) of the declaring class is used as a "
"logger name, for example, `org.jboss.logging.Logger.getLogger(SimpleBean."
"class)` will be used."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case, the name _foo_ is used as a logger name, for example, `org."
"jboss.logging.Logger.getLogger(\"foo\")` will be used."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The logger instances are cached internally.\n"
"Therefore, when a logger is injected, for example, into a `@RequestScoped` "
"bean, it is shared for all bean instances to avoid possible performance "
"penalties associated with logger instantiation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use log levels"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"{project-name} provides different log levels, which helps developers to "
"control the amount of information logged based on the severity of the events."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "Available log levels:"
msgstr ""

msgid "OFF"
msgstr ""

msgid "A special level used in configuration to turn off logging."
msgstr ""

msgid "FATAL"
msgstr ""

msgid "A critical service failure or total inability to handle any requests."
msgstr ""

msgid "ERROR"
msgstr ""

msgid "A major issue in processing or an inability to complete a request."
msgstr ""

msgid "WARN"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A non-critical service error or problem that might not require immediate "
"correction."
msgstr ""

msgid "INFO"
msgstr ""

msgid "Service lifecycle events or other important infrequent information."
msgstr ""

msgid "DEBUG"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Additional information about lifecycle events or events not tied to specific "
"requests, useful for debugging."
msgstr ""

msgid "TRACE"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Detailed per-request debugging information, potentially at a very high "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

msgid "ALL"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A special level to turn on logging for all messages, including custom levels."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also configure the following levels for applications and libraries "
"that use link:https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/logging/"
"Level.html[`java.util.logging`]:"
msgstr ""

msgid "SEVERE"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **ERROR**."
msgstr ""

msgid "WARNING"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **WARN**."
msgstr ""

msgid "CONFIG"
msgstr ""

msgid "Service configuration information."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINE"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **DEBUG**."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINER"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **TRACE**."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINEST"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Increased debug output compared to `TRACE`, which might have a higher "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

msgid "The mapping between the levels"
msgstr ""

msgid "Numerical level value"
msgstr ""

msgid "Standard level name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Equivalent `java.util.logging` (JUL) level name"
msgstr ""

msgid "1100"
msgstr ""

msgid "Not applicable"
msgstr ""

msgid "1000"
msgstr ""

msgid "900"
msgstr ""

msgid "800"
msgstr ""

msgid "700"
msgstr ""

msgid "500"
msgstr ""

msgid "400"
msgstr ""

msgid "300"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configure the log level, category, and format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JBoss Logging, integrated into {project-name}, offers a unified "
"configuration for all <<logging-apis,supported logging APIs>> through a "
"single configuration file that sets up all available extensions.\n"
"To adjust runtime logging, modify the `application.properties` file."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you set the log level to below `DEBUG`, you must also adjust the "
"minimum log level.\n"
"This setting might be applied either globally with the `quarkus.log.min-"
"level` configuration property, or per category:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This sets a floor level for which Quarkus needs to generate supporting code.\n"
"The minimum log level must be set at build time so that Quarkus can open the "
"door to optimization opportunities where logging on unusable levels can be "
"elided."
msgstr ""

msgid "An example from native execution:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting `INFO` as the minimum logging level sets lower-level checks, such as "
"`isTraceEnabled`, to `false`.\n"
"This identifies code like `if(logger.isDebug()) callMethod();` that will "
"never be executed and mark it as \"dead.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you add these properties on the command line, ensure the `\"` character "
"is escaped properly:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All potential properties are listed in the "
"<<loggingConfigurationReference,logging configuration reference>> section."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging categories"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Logging is configured on a per-category basis, with each category being "
"configured independently.\n"
"Configuration for a category applies recursively to all subcategories unless "
"there is a more specific subcategory configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The parent of all logging categories is called the \"root category.\"\n"
"As the ultimate parent, this category might contain a configuration that "
"applies globally to all other categories.\n"
"This includes the globally configured handlers and formatters."
msgstr ""

msgid "An example of a global configuration that applies to all categories:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this example, the root category is configured to use two named handlers: "
"`con` and `mylog`."
msgstr ""

msgid "An example of a per-category configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This example shows how you can configure the minimal log level on the "
"categories `org.apache.kafka.clients` and `org.apache.kafka.common.utils`."
msgstr ""

msgid "For more information, see <<loggingConfigurationReference>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to configure something extra for a specific category, create a "
"named handler like `quarkus.log.handler.[console|file|syslog].<your-handler-"
"name>.*` and set it up for that category by using `quarkus.log.category.<my-"
"category>.handlers`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An example use case can be a desire to use a different timestamp format for "
"log messages which are saved to a file than the format used for other "
"handlers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For further demonstration, see the outputs of the <<category-named-handlers-"
"example,Attaching named handlers to a category>> example."
msgstr ""

msgid "Property Name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".level"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"INFO footnote:[Some extensions might define customized default log levels "
"for certain categories to reduce log noise by default.\n"
"Setting the log level in configuration will override any extension-defined "
"log levels.]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The level to use to configure the category named `<category-name>`.\n"
"The quotes are necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".min-level"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The minimum logging level to use to configure the category named `<category-"
"name>`.\n"
"The quotes are necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".use-parent-handlers"
msgstr ""

msgid "true"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specify whether this logger should send its output to its parent logger."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".handlers=[<handler>]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"empty footnote:[By default, the configured category gets the same handlers "
"attached as the one on the root logger.]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The names of the handlers that you want to attach to a specific category."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `.` symbol separates the specific parts in the configuration property.\n"
"The quotes in the property name are used as a required escape to keep "
"category specifications, such as `quarkus.log.category.\"io.quarkus.smallrye."
"jwt\".level=TRACE`, intact."
msgstr ""

msgid "Root logger configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The root logger category is handled separately, and is configured by using "
"the following properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.level"
msgstr ""

msgid "The default log level for every log category."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.min-level"
msgstr ""

msgid "The default minimum log level for every log category."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The parent category is examined if no level configuration exists for a given "
"logger category."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The root logger configuration is used if no specific configurations are "
"provided for the category and any of its parent categories."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Although the root logger's handlers are usually configured directly via "
"`quarkus.log.console`, `quarkus.log.file` and `quarkus.log.syslog`, it can "
"nonetheless have additional named handlers attached to it using the `quarkus."
"log.handlers` property."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"{project-name} uses a pattern-based logging formatter that generates human-"
"readable text logs by default, but you can also configure the format for "
"each log handler by using a dedicated property."
msgstr ""

msgid "For the console handler, the property is `quarkus.log.console.format`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The logging format string supports the following symbols:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Symbol"
msgstr ""

msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

msgid "%%"
msgstr ""

msgid "`%`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders a simple `%` character."
msgstr ""

msgid "%c"
msgstr ""

msgid "Category"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the category name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%C"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source class"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the source class name.footnote:calc[Format sequences which examine "
"caller information might affect performance]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%d{xxx}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Date"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders a date with the given date format string, which uses the syntax "
"defined by `java.text.SimpleDateFormat`."
msgstr ""

msgid "%e"
msgstr ""

msgid "Exception"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the thrown exception, if any."
msgstr ""

msgid "%F"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source file"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the source file name.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%h"
msgstr ""

msgid "Host name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the system simple host name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%H"
msgstr ""

msgid "Qualified host name"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the system's fully qualified host name, which might be the same as "
"the simple host name, depending on operating system configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "%i"
msgstr ""

msgid "Process ID"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the current process PID."
msgstr ""

msgid "%l"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source location"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the source location information, which includes source file name, "
"line number, class name, and method name.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%L"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source line"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the source line number.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%m"
msgstr ""

msgid "Full Message"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the log message plus exception (if any)."
msgstr ""

msgid "%M"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source method"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the source method name.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%n"
msgstr ""

msgid "Newline"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the platform-specific line separator string."
msgstr ""

msgid "%N"
msgstr ""

msgid "Process name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the name of the current process."
msgstr ""

msgid "%p"
msgstr ""

msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the log level of the message."
msgstr ""

msgid "%r"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative time"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Render the time in milliseconds since the start of the application log."
msgstr ""

msgid "%s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Simple message"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders just the log message, with no exception trace."
msgstr ""

msgid "%t"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thread name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the thread name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%t{id}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thread ID"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the thread ID."
msgstr ""

msgid "%z{<zone name>}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Time zone"
msgstr ""

msgid "Set the time zone of the output to `<zone name>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "%X{<MDC property name>}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mapped Diagnostic Context Value"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the value from Mapped Diagnostic Context."
msgstr ""

msgid "%X"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mapped Diagnostic Context Values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders all the values from Mapped Diagnostic Context in format `{property."
"key=property.value}`."
msgstr ""

msgid "%x"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nested Diagnostics context values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders all the values from Nested Diagnostics Context in format `{value1."
"value2}`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alternative console logging formats"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Changing the console log format is useful, for example, when the console "
"output of the Quarkus application is captured by a service that processes "
"and stores the log information for later analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "JSON logging format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-logging-json` extension might be employed to add support for "
"the JSON logging format and its related configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add this extension to your build file as the following snippet illustrates:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the presence of this extension replaces the output format "
"configuration from the console configuration, and the format string and the "
"color settings (if any) are ignored.\n"
"The other console configuration items, including those that control "
"asynchronous logging and the log level, will continue to be applied."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For some, it will make sense to use humanly readable (unstructured) logging "
"in dev mode and JSON logging (structured) in production mode.\n"
"This can be achieved using different profiles, as shown in the following "
"configuration."
